# Production build settings. Committed on purpose — there is nothing secret
# here, and the value matters enough to pin in the repo rather than leave to a
# dashboard setting someone has to remember.
#
# The API base stays RELATIVE. In production the browser only ever talks to the
# Vercel domain, which rewrites /api/* through to Railway (see vercel.json).
# That keeps the auth cookies first-party, so SameSite=Lax keeps working and
# Safari/Brave third-party-cookie blocking can't sign users out.
#
# Pointing this at the Railway URL directly WILL break login: the cookie
# becomes cross-site and Lax stops sending it. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
VITE_API_URL=/api/v1
